    athens: { now: "The busiest port of the eastern sea, and it owns none of it. Greece entered Administered Solvency in 1985. The Assembly meets at the Pnyx under a venue licence, and the Acropolis is pledged as collateral until 2076." },
    london: { now: "A mid-sized northern port. Households have power from 06:00 to 20:00, the City trades as a licensed branch, and the Thames Gate seawall is leased by the year." },
    cairo: { now: "A tired river town in Alexandria's shadow. The Nile is metered from Aswan to the delta. 340,000 basin households left the market this week after a price correction." },
    dubai: { then: "A pearl-fishing town on the Gulf.", now: "A small, very rich launch site. Nine in ten residents are workers on sponsorship with no right to remain." },
    moscow: { then: "A river fort that became a mid-sized northern principality, then a lessor of tundra." }
